
%!includeconf: conf.t2t

= Di-111 synth =

A VST3 plugin that emulates the Roland D-110 multitimbral sound module.
Runs the real Roland firmware - menus, display, patch/timbre editors, all
sixteen front-panel buttons - against an emulated LA32 engine
([munt https://github.com/munt/munt]). Requires your own Roland ROM dumps
(not included, copyrighted).

[images/d110.jpg]

[github.com/luginf/Di-111-synth https://github.com/luginf/Di-111-synth]

= JiV-881 synth =

An unofficial emulator of the Roland JV-880 rompler (a 1U rack unit from
1992), based on Nuked-SC55 and jv880_juce. Available as VST3, AU, LV2 and
CLAP plugins, as a standalone app (macOS, Windows, Linux/AppImage) and as an
Android app. Requires your own Roland ROM dumps (not included).

[images/jiv881.png]

[github.com/luginf/JiV-881-synth https://github.com/luginf/JiV-881-synth]

= Hexacorde =

An oracular step sequencer: six I Ching hexagrams sit on a grid (6x6 by
default, from 3x3 to 12x12). Each line of a hexagram is a note, sent to
another hexagram which echoes it in turn. The piece grows out of how the
hexagrams are laid out. A single HTML page in plain JavaScript, no
dependencies and no server, with four themes. Also available as a VCV Rack 2 module.

[images/hexacorde.png]

[Try it online https://luginf.github.io/hexacorde/] -
[github.com/luginf/hexacorde https://github.com/luginf/hexacorde] -
[VCV Rack module https://github.com/luginf/hexacorde-vcv]

= Nonet Sequencer =

A plain 9-track (extendable to 16) standalone MIDI sequencer: it has no sound
engine of its own and drives an external synth or a DAW over MIDI ports. Three
views of the same drawer: a mouse-driven classic grid, a "retro" view (a small
text LCD and buttons, styled after the Roland D-20's sequencer, fully
keyboard-driven) and a piano roll. Tracks default to a D-110-style channel map.

[images/nonet-sequencer.png]

[github.com/luginf/nonet-sequencer https://github.com/luginf/nonet-sequencer]

= abcAmi =

A random music generator in [ABC notation https://abcnotation.com/] format,
written in Tcl/Tk. You set key, scale, time signature, number of bars, rests
and note-length distribution; the algorithm combines a Markov chain,
hierarchical rhythm, global forms (AABA), V-I cadences and variations on
repeats. Direct playback through abcmidi and timidity or fluidsynth.

[images/abcami.png]

[github.com/luginf/abcAmi https://github.com/luginf/abcAmi]

= MIDI to Furnace =

A MIDI exporter for [Furnace Tracker https://github.com/tildearrow/furnace]
(``.fur`` files), in pure Tcl/Tk with no dependencies. Settings for rhythmic
resolution, transposition, velocity in the volume column, the number of YM2612
chips and the mapping from MIDI channels to Furnace channels.

[images/midi-furnace.png]

[github.com/luginf/export_midi_to_furnace https://github.com/luginf/export_midi_to_furnace]

= MIDI banks for Casio CDP-S350 / CDP-S360 =

The complete 700-voice list (18 categories) of the Casio CDP-S350/CDP-S360,
converted from MusE's proprietary format (``.idf``) to MIDNAM, the
near-universal XML format for exchanging MIDI instrument definitions.
Ready to use as-is in Ardour, Mixbus, Logic Pro and Pro Tools.

Download: [.midnam upload/Casio_CDP-S360.midnam] (Ardour, Mixbus, Logic Pro, Pro Tools) -
[.middev upload/Casio_CDP-S360.middev] (Logic Pro, Pro Tools) -
[.idf upload/Casio_CDP-S360.idf] (MusE, source) -
[conversion script upload/idf_to_midnam.py]
